1
00:00:01,565 --> 00:00:04,809
The Mysterious Transfer Student

2
00:00:11,448 --> 00:00:12,739
This is Blue Cop.

3
00:00:12,739 --> 00:00:15,275
I have yet to find Heavy Iron's vehicle.

4
00:00:15,275 --> 00:00:17,475
I will resume my patrol.

5
00:00:21,763 --> 00:00:25,471
No sign of any large trailers here either, over.

6
00:00:27,466 --> 00:00:28,931
Ugh...

7
00:00:30,646 --> 00:00:33,521
How can such a big guy be so hard to find?

8
00:00:33,521 --> 00:00:36,630
Maybe he has the power to disappear, like someone else we know.

9
00:00:36,630 --> 00:00:37,567
You two!

10
00:00:38,176 --> 00:00:40,533
Now's not the time to be slacking off!

11
00:00:42,289 --> 00:00:43,932
You startled me!

12
00:00:43,932 --> 00:00:48,554
Alright, alright! Let's get back to the mission! Hup-two, Hup-two! Hurry up!

13
00:00:48,554 --> 00:00:49,795
Alright, we're coming.

14
00:00:49,795 --> 00:00:52,759
Ugh... that naggy little brat.

15
00:00:52,759 --> 00:00:54,368
No complaining!

16
00:00:54,368 --> 00:00:57,368
Everyone, please keep up the search.

17
00:00:57,878 --> 00:00:58,753
Roger that!

18
00:00:59,503 --> 00:00:59,503
Ugh...

19
00:01:00,298 --> 00:01:01,899
They say that sighing chases away good fortune.

20
00:01:02,000 --> 00:01:05,090
Thanks.

21
00:01:05,884 --> 00:01:06,569
That'll be four dollars.

22
00:01:07,000 --> 00:01:09,000
You're charging me for it?!

23
00:01:09,200 --> 00:01:11,287
I was just kidding. Here.

24
00:01:12,561 --> 00:01:14,864
I know how you must be feeling.

25
00:01:14,864 --> 00:01:20,341
We can't find Heavy Iron, who defeated Blue Cop.

26
00:01:20,341 --> 00:01:24,771
And we don't know who the Metal Cardbot who helped us out was.

27
00:01:24,771 --> 00:01:27,509
So, are you telling me to be patient,

28
00:01:27,509 --> 00:01:29,682
and that they'll all turn up in due time?

29
00:01:29,682 --> 00:01:31,965
No, I think we'd better hurry.

30
00:01:32,626 --> 00:01:34,984
Looks like it's going to rain.

31
00:01:35,496 --> 00:01:38,906
Oh no! I gotta get going then!

32
00:01:38,906 --> 00:01:41,734
When everyone gets back, tell them to get inside the garage.

33
00:01:41,734 --> 00:01:43,424
Alright. Take care!

34
00:01:43,424 --> 00:01:44,269
Later!

35
00:01:53,200 --> 00:01:55,384
Is all this rain also because I sighed?

36
00:01:59,216 --> 00:02:01,105
Hey you!

37
00:02:01,105 --> 00:02:03,590
Watch where you're driving, will ya?!

38
00:02:09,651 --> 00:02:13,638
Alright class, settle down! We have a new student joining us today!

39
00:02:13,638 --> 00:02:14,610
Come on in.

40
00:02:18,187 --> 00:02:19,937
Please introduce yourself.

41
00:02:20,353 --> 00:02:22,146
My name is Crest.

42
00:02:23,771 --> 00:02:25,389
Nice to meet you all.

43
00:02:25,670 --> 00:02:27,764
Ah!

44
00:02:28,162 --> 00:02:31,340
Ah! He's so handsome!

45
00:02:31,340 --> 00:02:33,312
He'll make my channel blow up!

46
00:02:34,275 --> 00:02:37,882
What are they all squealing about, huh?!

47
00:02:38,949 --> 00:02:41,728
He's not so handsome. Am I right, Jun?

48
00:02:41,977 --> 00:02:45,250
To real men, looks aren't important! It's what's on the inside that counts!

49
00:02:45,250 --> 00:02:46,531
Right, Anna?

50
00:02:46,870 --> 00:02:50,621
Ah... good looks really are everything!

51
00:02:50,621 --> 00:02:53,651
That's enough, everyone! Now let's see...

52
00:02:53,651 --> 00:02:55,896
You can go sit behind Vance over there.

53
00:02:55,896 --> 00:02:57,280
Thank you very much, teacher.

54
00:02:58,514 --> 00:03:00,770
That's a nice watch you're wearing.

55
00:03:00,787 --> 00:03:03,163
y-yeah...

56
00:03:04,597 --> 00:03:08,770
Let's get started with the lesson, then. Please open your textbooks to page 48.

57
00:03:10,465 --> 00:03:12,447
Crest, where did you move here from?

58
00:03:12,447 --> 00:03:14,461
Eastpolis.

59
00:03:14,461 --> 00:03:16,508
I had to move here because of my parents' jobs.

60
00:03:16,508 --> 00:03:20,425
I'm not familiar with this town yet. Do you think you could show me around sometime?

61
00:03:20,425 --> 00:03:23,103
-Of course! 
-Any time!

62
00:03:23,103 --> 00:03:24,209
Thank you, I appreciate it.

63
00:03:26,818 --> 00:03:29,966
Hmph! Just look at that jerk. He's already making moves!

64
00:03:30,437 --> 00:03:32,199
Let's see how he likes this!

65
00:03:36,127 --> 00:03:36,864
Watch out!

66
00:03:39,776 --> 00:03:41,340
Huh?!

67
00:03:41,686 --> 00:03:43,632
You should be more careful, Vance.

68
00:03:43,632 --> 00:03:45,331
How do you know my name?!

69
00:03:45,331 --> 00:03:49,204
I already know everyone's names. I memorized the list of students enrolled here.

70
00:03:49,204 --> 00:03:50,932
C'mon, that's a lie!

71
00:03:51,430 --> 00:03:53,275
I'm not lying, Lavi.

72
00:03:53,275 --> 00:03:55,110
That's Theo behind you.

73
00:03:55,110 --> 00:03:56,173
And Anna...

74
00:03:56,173 --> 00:03:56,965
Vera...

75
00:03:56,965 --> 00:03:57,812
Kate...

76
00:03:57,812 --> 00:03:58,807
Helena...

77
00:03:58,807 --> 00:03:59,819
And Naomi.

78
00:03:59,819 --> 00:04:01,979
Wow, that's amazing!

79
00:04:01,979 --> 00:04:03,812
Just give me back the ball!

80
00:04:03,812 --> 00:04:05,193
Take it from me, then.

81
00:04:05,401 --> 00:04:05,870
It's mine now!

82
00:04:08,036 --> 00:04:09,634
Stop moving!

83
00:04:15,780 --> 00:04:16,483
It went in!

84
00:04:16,483 --> 00:04:17,994
Such a good shot!

85
00:04:19,225 --> 00:04:20,831
Just a little trick I learned.

86
00:04:20,831 --> 00:04:22,451
Hey Vance, wait up!

87
00:04:22,716 --> 00:04:24,766
Did I overdo it?

88
00:04:25,550 --> 00:04:28,225
Not even Vance could do a thing...

89
00:04:29,310 --> 00:04:30,899
So his name is Crest?

90
00:04:36,283 --> 00:04:38,370
You find the new kid suspicious?

91
00:04:38,370 --> 00:04:41,480
There's something about the way he looks and acts...

92
00:04:41,480 --> 00:04:43,199
It just doesn't seem right.

93
00:04:43,199 --> 00:04:45,750
Hehe! Are you sure you're not just jealous that Anna is into him?

94
00:04:45,750 --> 00:04:50,579
Argh, it's not that! He took an interest in my Metal Breath too!

95
00:04:50,579 --> 00:04:52,672
Something does seem a little off...

96
00:04:52,672 --> 00:04:54,930
What are you two talking about?

97
00:04:54,930 --> 00:04:56,163
Aaah!

98
00:04:56,699 --> 00:04:59,350
C-Crest, what are you doing here?

99
00:04:59,350 --> 00:05:01,925
I'm sorry, I hope now's not a bad time?

100
00:05:01,925 --> 00:05:04,500
Anna, did you bring him here?

101
00:05:04,500 --> 00:05:05,879
Well, of course!

102
00:05:05,879 --> 00:05:07,831
Crest said he has something he wants to talk to you about.

103
00:05:07,831 --> 00:05:09,947
You should have said something before coming!

104
00:05:09,947 --> 00:05:13,461
Why? You'd just be riding around on your bike anyway.

105
00:05:13,461 --> 00:05:17,173
This isn't a playground for kids. You should all head home already.

106
00:05:17,173 --> 00:05:18,920
But Jun can stay?!

107
00:05:18,920 --> 00:05:22,961
I never gave him permission either. He just barges in whenever he wants!

108
00:05:22,961 --> 00:05:27,213
Wah? Now you're just being mean, Uncle Edo! You told me I could come hang out any time-

109
00:05:27,213 --> 00:05:30,143
T-That's for sale! You shouldn't touch it!

110
00:05:30,143 --> 00:05:32,276
I'm sorry, I haven't seen a car like this before-

111
00:05:32,276 --> 00:05:37,000
Haha, no way, are you serious?! There are so many of these c-cars around here!

112
00:05:37,000 --> 00:05:37,875
Y-yeah...

113
00:05:37,875 --> 00:05:41,747
You only moved here recently, so that's probably why it's new to you...

114
00:05:41,747 --> 00:05:44,814
It looks a lot like the R48 used in highway patrol,

115
00:05:44,814 --> 00:05:47,295
but the shape of the hood and exhaust pipes are different.

116
00:05:47,295 --> 00:05:51,298
Woah, Crest! You're an expert on cars too?!

117
00:05:51,298 --> 00:05:55,915
Well, this is a custom vehicle. It's been modified according to the owner's specifications.

118
00:05:55,915 --> 00:05:58,718
Hmm... Is that so?

119
00:05:58,718 --> 00:06:01,713
Haha, y-yeah! That's why!

120
00:06:01,713 --> 00:06:03,891
But what did you want to talk about?

121
00:06:03,891 --> 00:06:06,740
Sorry for the sudden request, but I have a favor to ask.

122
00:06:06,740 --> 00:06:10,759
Just say the word! Crest can ask for anything he wants!

123
00:06:10,759 --> 00:06:12,367
That's not for you to decide!

124
00:06:12,367 --> 00:06:13,826
Aah! Guys!

125
00:06:13,826 --> 00:06:15,213
What's wrong, Anna?!

126
00:06:16,584 --> 00:06:17,860
W-what is it?!

127
00:06:21,899 --> 00:06:22,973
That's...

128
00:06:22,973 --> 00:06:25,242
That's the Metal Cardbot from the other day!

129
00:06:25,242 --> 00:06:27,329
The views will be out of this world!

130
00:06:27,329 --> 00:06:31,422
Bring me Blue Cop. I know he's hiding here somewhere!

131
00:06:31,422 --> 00:06:34,377
W-what? Lemme see who we're dealing with!

132
00:06:34,377 --> 00:06:37,487
Hang on. We'll be discovered if we make a move now.

133
00:06:43,136 --> 00:06:46,425
Come out and show yourself, you coward!

134
00:06:47,790 --> 00:06:51,120
I'm back. I didn't find any leads either.

135
00:06:53,807 --> 00:06:54,946
Isn't that...!

136
00:06:54,946 --> 00:06:56,889
What's going on, who is this guy?

137
00:06:57,146 --> 00:07:00,475
H-Hello, first responders! Over here!

138
00:07:02,899 --> 00:07:04,170
Ah! O-oh, right!

139
00:07:04,492 --> 00:07:05,961
Come on, let's go!

140
00:07:05,961 --> 00:07:07,754
But I'm not even hurt!

141
00:07:07,754 --> 00:07:09,475
Uh... just get in for now!

142
00:07:09,475 --> 00:07:10,865
Jun? Aren't you coming?!

143
00:07:10,865 --> 00:07:13,411
W-well.. uhh... there's no space for me in there!

144
00:07:13,411 --> 00:07:18,161
I have my bike, so I'll go by myself, o-okay?

145
00:07:18,161 --> 00:07:20,151
Theo, take care of them, okay?

146
00:07:20,151 --> 00:07:22,204
Okay. You be careful too.

147
00:07:27,322 --> 00:07:28,487
The coast is clear, Blue Cop!

148
00:07:36,692 --> 00:07:38,600
You, identify yourself.

149
00:07:38,600 --> 00:07:42,757
My name is Wild Guardy. And I am going to be king of the Metal Cardbots!

150
00:07:42,757 --> 00:07:45,665
Ha! King of us? What a joke.

151
00:07:45,665 --> 00:07:48,680
Hang on! Wild Guardy. Weren't you on our side?

152
00:07:48,680 --> 00:07:51,831
Yeah! You helped us in the battle against Heavy Iron, remember?

153
00:07:51,831 --> 00:07:57,213
Hmph. Do not be mistaken. I just didn't want a bunch of weaklings to steal my victory.

154
00:07:57,213 --> 00:07:58,417
What?

155
00:07:58,417 --> 00:08:01,540
The one who will take you down shall be I;

156
00:08:01,540 --> 00:08:02,608
The great, Wild Guardy!

157
00:08:04,954 --> 00:08:06,334
Jun!

158
00:08:13,985 --> 00:08:15,826
Metal Breath, pickup!

159
00:08:17,605 --> 00:08:19,490
Blue Cop, setup!

160
00:08:40,653 --> 00:08:43,307
Blue Cop! Burst Shot!

161
00:08:44,889 --> 00:08:46,619
Burst Shot!

162
00:08:50,312 --> 00:08:51,754
Way to go!

163
00:08:57,970 --> 00:09:00,288
Yeah well, that thing's got nothing on my shield!

164
00:09:00,288 --> 00:09:02,870
I hope that's not all you've got?

165
00:09:02,870 --> 00:09:04,331
Of course not!

166
00:09:04,692 --> 00:09:07,918
Blue Cop! Thunderbolt Smash!

167
00:09:11,548 --> 00:09:12,596
Thunderbolt...

168
00:09:12,677 --> 00:09:13,600
Smash!!

169
00:09:27,562 --> 00:09:30,360
Thunderbolt Smash didn't work.

170
00:09:30,494 --> 00:09:36,619
My shield has been tempered by the magma of planet Machina for over thousands of years.

171
00:09:36,619 --> 00:09:38,812
Your feeble attacks are useless!

172
00:09:46,427 --> 00:09:49,250
Wild... Slash!

173
00:09:56,850 --> 00:09:57,970
Blue Cop!

174
00:09:58,567 --> 00:10:00,951
Hey! You alright?

175
00:10:02,783 --> 00:10:04,258
Jun! Tag me in!

176
00:10:04,527 --> 00:10:05,850
It's no use.

177
00:10:05,850 --> 00:10:07,667
You're no match for me.

178
00:10:07,667 --> 00:10:09,663
Huh? What did you say?

179
00:10:12,129 --> 00:10:15,590
Haaaaaaaa haa!

180
00:10:20,697 --> 00:10:19,697
///

181
00:10:23,125 --> 00:10:24,595
Are you okay, Blue bro?

182
00:10:24,595 --> 00:10:27,537
Since when did you and Blue Cop become brothers?

183
00:10:27,537 --> 00:10:31,533
Another pest has shown up.

184
00:10:31,533 --> 00:10:34,499
I'll be waiting for our next showdown, Blue Cop.

185
00:10:43,331 --> 00:10:45,570
Come back, Wild Guardy...!

186
00:10:45,903 --> 00:10:47,320
Blue Cop!

187
00:10:49,642 --> 00:10:51,354
B-Blue Cop, are you alright?!

188
00:10:51,354 --> 00:10:53,499
Say something, Blue Cop!

